      "text": "## Your Bicycle\n\nYour bicycle is **blue**.\n\nThis was stated directly in a single message on 2026-11-01: *\"My bicycle is blue.\"* There is only one record of the bicycle's colour in the memory bank, and no subsequent statement changes or contradicts it. Searches for any alternative colour (e.g. red, green) or any update/change to the bicycle colour returned no additional facts.\n\n### Is the bicycle colour unresolved?\n\n**No — it is resolved.** The colour is clearly and unambiguously **blue**. There is exactly one fact about the bicycle's colour, it carries no conflicting counterpart, and nothing later supersedes it. There is no ambiguity to reconcile here.\n\n## Your Coffee Preference\n\nYou prefer **espresso**. This was also stated in the same 2026-11-01 message: *\"I now prefer espresso.\"* The phrasing (\"now prefer\") suggests this may reflect a shift from an earlier preference, but the memory bank contains no record of what your previous coffee preference was — only the current one (espresso) is documented.\n\n## Your Hobby\n\nYour hobby is **pottery**. The memory bank records that *\"The user started pottery\"* on 2026-11-01. This is the only hobby mentioned in the available data.\n\n## Summary\n\n| Item | Value | Source Date |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bicycle colour | **Blue** | 2026-11-01 |\n| Coffee preference | **Espresso** | 2026-11-01 |\n| Hobby | **Pottery** | 2026-11-01 |\n| Bicycle colour resolved? | **Yes — blue, no conflict** | — |",
